'''Lion's Roar''' is a [[unique]] {{il|Granite Flask}}.

{{Item acquisition}}

==Ruthless mode==
Utility Flasks cannot gain charges while active in [[Ruthless mode]]. This flask also has a flask duration of 4.00 seconds instead.

==Legacy variants==
Lion's Roar has [[legacy variant]]s.

{{legacy variant table header}}
{{legacy variant table row|3.15.0
|
* Adds Knockback to Melee Attacks during Flask effect
* Knocks Back Enemies in an Area when you use a Flask
* 75% chance to cause Enemies to Flee on use
* {{c|mod|(20-25)% more Melee Physical Damage during effect}}{{efn|name=Reroll legacy explicit }}
}}
{{legacy variant table row|3.0.0
|
* Adds Knockback to Melee Attacks during Flask effect
* Knocks Back Enemies in an Area when you use a Flask
* 75% chance to cause Enemies to Flee on use 
* {{c|mod|(30-35)% more Melee Physical Damage during effect}} {{efn|name=Reroll legacy explicit }}
}}
{{legacy variant table row|2.2.0
|
* {{c|mod|(70-100)% increased Charges used}}
* Adds Knockback to Melee Attacks during Flask effect
* Knocks Back Enemies in an Area when you use a Flask
* 75% chance to cause Enemies to Flee on use
* {{c|mod|30% more Melee Physical Damage during effect}}{{efn|name=Reroll legacy explicit }}
}}
{{Legacy variant table end}}

The {{c|mod|increased Charges used}} mod (from pre-2.2.0 version) cannot be removed as the game developer DID NOT set a new 0 default value to that mod (sometimes they did for other legacy unique item). The pre-2.2.0 version ''can'' have mod value of (30-35)% for the mod {{c|mod|#% more Melee Physical Damage during effect}}, if the player had used a {{il|Divine Orb}} during the period from [[version 2.2.0]] to before [[version 3.0.0|3.0.0]] (i.e. [[version 2.6.3]]), making it a hybrid variant. However, since the current range is (7-10)%, such hybrid variant is useless to create currently, so that it is not recommended to [[Divine Orb|divine]] it.

